    "answer": "As an expert in Indonesian immigration law, I can confirm that securing a working stay permit for a foreign director involves a strict, multi-agency national procedure governed primarily by **Peraturan Pemerintah Nomor 34 Tahun 2021 (PP 34/2021)** on the Utilization of Foreign Workers and **Permenkumham Nomor 22 Tahun 2023** regarding visa classifications [1, 2]. \n\nWhile you referenced the standard **E23 Working KITAS**, under the current immigration index system, a foreign Director specifically falls under the **E25B (Director KITAS)** index, which still requires the same foundational work authorization (RPTKA) from the Ministry of Manpower (Kemnaker) [3]. \n\nTo process this work permit, the sponsoring PT PMA (Foreign Investment Company) and the foreign worker must provide the following documentation:\n\n**1. Corporate Documents Required from the Sponsoring PT PMA:**\nThe company acts as the mandatory sponsor and must provide robust corporate compliance records [4, 5]:\n*   **NIB (Nomor Induk Berusaha):** Must be active in the OSS system and contain the KBLI (business sector code) matching the director's specific job title [4, 6].\n*   **Deed of Establishment & Amendments (Akta Pendirian PT + Perubahan terakhir):** Accompanied by the Ministry of Law and Human Rights approval decree (*SK Kemenkumham*) [4, 5].\n*   **Company Tax ID (NPWP Perusahaan)** [4, 5].\n*   **WLKP (Wajib Lapor Ketenagakerjaan Perusahaan):** A mandatory and up-to-date company employment report [5].\n*   **BPJS Ketenagakerjaan Report:** Proof of active social security enrollment for the company's local Indonesian employees [5].\n*   **Company Organizational Chart (Bagan Organisasi):** Visually demonstrating the foreign director's position within the company hierarchy [4, 7].\n*   **Statement of Companion Worker (Surat Pernyataan Pendampingan):** A formal commitment to appoint a local Indonesian worker (TKI Pendamping) for knowledge transfer [4].\n*   **Approved RPTKA (Rencana Penggunaan Tenaga Kerja Asing):** The formal work authorization plan approved by Kemnaker, which replaced the physical IMTA document [1, 8].\n\n**2. Personal Documents Required from the Foreign Director:**\n*   **Original Passport:** Must have a minimum residual validity of 18 months (recommended for a 12-month KITAS) [5, 9].\n*   **Curriculum Vitae (CV):** In English or Indonesian, demonstrating at least 5 years of relevant professional experience for the specific sector [5, 9].\n*   **Academic Degree/Diploma (Ijazah):** Must be highly relevant to the position. For foreign degrees, it must be translated and legalized via Apostille or by the Indonesian Embassy/Consulate (KBRI) [5, 9, 10].\n*   **Health Insurance Policy:** Must be valid for use in Indonesia for the entire duration of the stay [9].\n*   **Health Certificate (Surat Keterangan Sehat):** A medical certificate confirming good health [5].\n*   **Police Clearance Certificate:** An equivalent of the Indonesian SKCK from the applicant's home country [5].\n*   **Photographs:** Recent 4x6 cm color passport photos with a red background (standard for Kemnaker and Imigrasi processing) [5, 10].\n\n**Critical Legal Restrictions (National Rules):**\nYou must ensure the Director title strictly complies with **Kepmenaker 228/2019** (Allowed Positions) and **Kepmenaker 349/2019** (Prohibited Positions). For example, a foreigner is strictly prohibited from holding the title of **\"Direktur Utama\" (Chief Executive Officer / General Director)** *unless* the PT PMA operates in the Mining Sector (KBLI 05-09) [11, 12]. In all other sectors, alternative titles such as *Direktur Operasional* or *Direktur Pengembangan Bisnis* must be used, provided they match the company's KBLI code [13].\n\n**Bali Local Procedures:**\nWhile the RPTKA approval and the E-Visa (VITAS) issuance are handled electronically at the national level in Jakarta, the final step—the biometric capture, physical KITAS issuance, and mandatory civil reporting (such as obtaining an STM from the police)—must be executed locally at the specific Immigration Office (Kantor Imigrasi) corresponding to the director's domicile in Bali (e.g., Kantor Imigrasi Ngurah Rai) [14, 15].",
