    "answer": "Under Indonesia's Positive Investment List (Perpres No. 10 of 2021), which operates in tandem with the Job Creation Law (Omnibus Law UU No. 6 of 2023) and the updated Risk-Based Licensing framework (PP No. 28 of 2025 replacing PP No. 5/2021), foreign investors can establish a PT PMA with 100% ownership in sectors classified as **TERBUKA** (Open) [1-3]. \n\nHere are the key KBLI codes that are officially **TERBUKA** for 100% PT PMA ownership:\n\n**Hospitality and Food & Beverage (F&B)**\n*   **KBLI 56101 (Restoran / Restaurants):** **TERBUKA** [4, 5].\n*   **KBLI 56103 (Bar):** **TERBUKA** [4, 5].\n*   **KBLI 55193 / 55194 (Vila / Commercial Villas):** **TERBUKA** [4, 6].\n*   **KBLI 55110 (Hotel Bintang / Star Hotels) & KBLI 55120 (Hotel Melati / Non-star Hotels):** **TERBUKA** [4]. \n*(Note: KBLI 55130 for Pondok Wisata / Homestays is strictly **TERTUTUP** and reserved exclusively for Indonesian citizens, making it 0% open to foreign ownership) [7, 8].*\n\n**Tourism, Wellness, and Recreation**\n*   **KBLI 79120 (Jasa Perjalanan Wisata / Tour Operators):** **TERBUKA** [9].\n*   **KBLI 93139 (Pusat Kesehatan dan Kebugaran / Fitness & Wellness Centers):** **TERBUKA** [9, 10].\n*   **KBLI 93199 (Aktivitas Olahraga Lainnya / Other Sports Activities such as surf schools):** **TERBUKA** [9, 10].\n\n**Education and Professional Services**\n*   **KBLI 85493 (Pendidikan Non-Formal Lainnya / Non-Formal Education like yoga teacher training):** **TERBUKA** [10, 11].\n*   **KBLI 74300 (Penerjemahan / Translation Services):** **TERBUKA** [12].\n*   **KBLI 70201 (Konsultasi Bisnis / Business Consulting):** **TERBUKA** [12].\n\n**Real Estate and Holding Companies**\n*   **KBLI 68200 (Aktivitas Real Estat atas Dasar Balas Jasa / Real Estate Management for a fee or contract):** **TERBUKA** [11].\n*   **KBLI 64210 (Aktivitas Perusahaan Induk / Holding Company):** **TERBUKA** [13].\n\n**Technology and Digital Economy**\n*   **KBLI 62010 (Sviluppo Software / Software Development):** **TERBUKA** [14].\n*   **KBLI 62193 (Aktivitas Pengembangan Aplikasi Berbasis Teknologi Blockchain):** **TERBUKA** [15].\n*   **KBLI 62194 (Aktivitas Pengembangan Komponen Dasar Kecerdasan Buatan / AI):** **TERBUKA** [16].\n\n**Retail and Trade**\n*   **KBLI 47630 (Toko Aksesoris / Accessory Shops) & KBLI 47762 (Toko Batik dan Kerajinan Tangan / Batik & Handicrafts):** **TERBUKA** [9, 17]. \n\n**Post-Omnibus Law Capital and Compliance Rules:**\nTo utilize any of these **TERBUKA** codes, your PT PMA must comply with the post-Omnibus Law capital mandates set forth in BKPM Regulation No. 5 of 2025. The minimum paid-up capital has been reduced to IDR 2.5 billion per company, which must be locked in the corporate bank account for 12 months for operational use [18-20]. However, the total investment commitment remains strictly greater than IDR 10 billion per 5-digit KBLI code and per project location, excluding land and buildings [18, 20]. \n\nUnder the continuous compliance model of PP 28/2025, realization of this capital must be consistently reported through the quarterly LKPM (Laporan Kegiatan Penanaman Modal) to maintain your business licenses and avoid automated system sanctions [19-21].",
