        "cited_text": "Implementation timeline and rollout phases The CoreTax implementation followed a carefully structured timeline, though not without challenges. The system's development began in earnest following the 2018 Presidential Regulation, with the LG CNS-Qualysoft Consortium selected as the primary contractor. Pre-implementation phase (December 16-31, 2024): This critical period allowed taxpayers to access the system for testing and familiarization purposes. Beginning December 24, 2024, taxpayers could log in to perform basic functions such as password reset and data verification. Official launch (January 1, 2025): CoreTax became fully operational for all tax obligations beginning with the January 2025 tax period. This marked the transition from the legacy system to the new platform for most core tax functions. Parallel operation period (January 2025 - ongoing): Recognizing initial implementation challenges, the DJP and Parliament agreed to operate CoreTax alongside legacy systems for certain functions. This includes continued use of DJP Online for annual tax return filing for 2024 tax year obligations and parallel operation of e-Faktur desktop applications for specific taxpayer categories. Phased migration: The complete transition to CoreTax for all functions is planned to occur gradually, with annual tax returns for the 2025 tax year (filed in 2026) being the first to be submitted exclusively through the new system."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "8449662f-a07d-4868-88c7-3f10f20ba520",
        "citation_number": 11,
        "cited_text": "Impact on businesses The implementation of CoreTax has fundamentally altered the tax reporting landscape for businesses operating in Indonesia. The most significant change involves the consolidation of previously separate reporting processes into a unified digital platform that demands new operational approaches from taxpayers. Businesses no longer need to navigate multiple applications for different tax functions. Where previously a company might use e-Faktur for VAT invoices, e-Billing for payments, and DJP Online for return filing, CoreTax integrates these functions into a single interface."
      },
