        "source_id": "8449662f-a07d-4868-88c7-3f10f20ba520",
        "citation_number": 12,
        "cited_text": "Core Functions and Objectives of the CoreTax System Download publications An Introduction to Doing Business in Indonesia 2026 CoreTax represents a comprehensive reimagining of tax administration , built around five core business processes that integrate previously separate functions: Registration and taxpayer management: The system introduces a unified approach to taxpayer registration, incorporating new features such as facial recognition for identity verification and automatic generation of Tax Identification Numbers (NPWP) for individuals using their National Identity Numbers (NIK). For businesses, the system streamlines the process of obtaining Taxable Entrepreneur (PKP) status and managing corporate tax obligations. Tax return management: CoreTax consolidates all tax return processes into a single platform, eliminating the need for multiple applications. The system automatically generates tax invoice serial numbers and provides real-time validation of submitted data. Processing times have been dramatically reduced, with tax return submission dropping from 29.28 seconds to just 3.93 seconds according to official DJP data. Payment processing: The system introduces three streamlined billing code generation schemes, including automated generation linked to tax return filing, payment of tax assessments, and self-service creation for specific obligations. A significant innovation is the introduction of a \"tax deposit\" feature, functioning like an e-wallet system that allows taxpayers to pre-fund their tax obligations. Taxpayer services: CoreTax provides comprehensive taxpayer account management through its Taxpayer Account Management (TAM) feature, offering a unified view of all tax-related information and transactions. This includes real-time access to payment histories, outstanding obligations, and compliance status. Compliance monitoring: The system integrates data from multiple sources, including population databases, third-party transaction records, and e-commerce platforms, enabling comprehensive compliance monitoring and reducing opportunities for tax evasion."
