    "references": [
      {
        "source_id": "cc368f26-9a0d-4f48-9a4d-c7dda436f18e",
        "citation_number": 1,
        "cited_text": "Related parties; The stages of the ALP; Transfer pricing techniques; Comparability analysis; Special transactions; and Secondary adjustments. The Ministry of Finance issued PMK-172 on December 29 2023, as the implementing regulation required by the Law on Harmonisation of Tax Regulations and Government Regulation No. 55 of 2022. PMK-172 revokes the three previous regulations issued by the Ministry of Finance. New transfer pricing rules under PMK-172 PMK-172 can be divided into six parts, in accordance with the transfer pricing compliance cycle."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "a16436de-3323-47d5-b5e2-0098ab6e2207",
        "citation_number": 2,
        "cited_text": "Acclime helps you set up, manage and advance your business in Indonesia and beyond. Talk to an expert Contents What is transfer pricing? The arm's length principle When do transfer pricing rules apply? Risk of transfer pricing adjustments High-level compliance obligations Indonesia's transfer pricing (TP) regime is among the most enforcement-active in South-East Asia. Governed by Minister of Finance Regulation No. 172 of 2023 (PMK-172), which took full effect for tax year 2024, the framework consolidates Indonesia's documentation, advance pricing agreement (APA) and mutual agreement procedure (MAP) rules into a single regulation aligned with the OECD Transfer Pricing Guidelines and BEPS Action 13."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "a16436de-3323-47d5-b5e2-0098ab6e2207",
        "citation_number": 3,
        "cited_text": "What is transfer pricing? Transfer pricing refers to the pricing of transactions between related parties within a multinational enterprise (MNE) group. Controlled transactions include the sale of goods, provision of services, licensing of intangible assets, intercompany loans and financial arrangements. Because related parties can set prices outside normal market conditions, tax authorities examine these prices to verify that profits are reported where economic activity and value creation actually occur."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "a16436de-3323-47d5-b5e2-0098ab6e2207",
        "citation_number": 4,
        "cited_text": "Where the CUP or CUT method can be applied with a similar degree of reliability as other methods, these approaches must be prioritised over the remaining methodologies. When do transfer pricing rules apply in Indonesia? TP obligations arise from the existence of a special relationship and, for documentation purposes, from meeting the applicable thresholds. However, the obligation to price on arm's length terms applies regardless of documentation thresholds. An entity below the documentation threshold remains exposed to DGT adjustments if its controlled transactions are not priced at arm's length."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "aa5a6e2a-ffff-4747-a36d-63d8860be233",
        "citation_number": 5,
        "cited_text": "exemption from transfer pricing documentation obligations? ☒ Yes ☐ No Article 16 of the Minister of Finance Regulation Number 172 of 2023 (in unofficial English translation) A taxpayer who meets the following criteria is exempt from transfer pricing documentation obligation: a. annual gross turnover in the preceding taxable year no more than IDR 50 billion; b. annual value of related party transaction in the preceding taxable year: 1. no more than IDR 20 billion for tangible goods transaction; or 2. no more than IDR 5 billion"
      },
      {
        "source_id": "b0ea1709-a9ac-46cb-9843-6cc8cc1ebdb1",
        "citation_number": 6,
        "cited_text": "Se la PT PMA effettua transazioni con PIHAK BERELASI (parti correlate — es. società madre estera, filiali, soci) deve rispettare le regole di Transfer Pricing (TP). [TAX-023] PRINCIPIO FONDAMENTALE: arm's length principle (kewajaran dan kelaziman) Le transazioni intercompany devono avvenire a prezzi di mercato. SOGLIA OBBLIGATORIA (PMK 213/2016): Obbligo di TP Documentation se: Transaksi dengan pihak berelasi > IDR 50 miliardi/anno, OPPURE Pembayaran ke tax haven countries > IDR 10 miliardi/anno, OPPURE Qualsiasi transazione con entità in paesi a bassa fiscalità"
      },
      {
        "source_id": "aa5a6e2a-ffff-4747-a36d-63d8860be233",
        "citation_number": 7,
        "cited_text": "for each of service provision, interest payment, utilization of intangible goods, or any other related party transactions; or c. have no related party transaction in a country or jurisdiction with income tax rate lower than the income tax rate as referred to in Article 17 of Income Tax Law. For Income Tax Rates as stated in the Income Tax Law, the rate has been changed in to the new rates in the Tax Harmonization Law Number 7 of 2021. The rates are mentioned in Article 17 point 1 Tax Harmonization Law Number 7 of 2021:"
      },
      {
        "source_id": "a16436de-3323-47d5-b5e2-0098ab6e2207",
        "citation_number": 8,
        "cited_text": "Under PMK-172, the requirements relating to Country-by-Country Reporting (CbCR) for domestic taxpayers have been revised. A taxpayer is now obligated to prepare a CbCR if it acts as the parent entity of a business group whose consolidated gross revenue reaches at least IDR 11 trillion in the fiscal year preceding the reporting year. This represents a shift from the previous rule under PMK-213, where the revenue threshold was assessed based on the same fiscal year being reported. The concept of a parent entity has also been updated. The current regulation determines parent entity status by reference to ownership, whereas the prior framework applied a control-based criterion. In addition, PMK-172 clarifies that taxpayers are permitted to submit a corrected CbCR if inaccuracies are identified in the original submission."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "b0ea1709-a9ac-46cb-9843-6cc8cc1ebdb1",
        "citation_number": 9,
        "cited_text": "DOCUMENTI TP RICHIESTI: Dokumen Induk (Master File) — profilo gruppo multinazionale Dokumen Lokal (Local File) — dettaglio transazioni in Indonesia Laporan per negara (Country-by-Country Report) — solo per gruppi con omzet consolidato > IDR 11 trilioni PRESENTAZIONE: Allegata alla SPT Tahunan Badan o su richiesta DJP. Per le piccole PT PMA con operatività solo in Indonesia e limitati rapporti intercompany, l'obbligo TP spesso non scatta. ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━"
