        "citation_number": 10,
        "cited_text": "PMK-172 introduces an obligation for taxpayers to perform a preliminary assessment for certain related party transactions (RPTs). This assessment must, among others, evaluate the commercial justification of the transaction and the anticipated economic benefits derived from it. The requirement applies to various types of transactions, including service arrangements, financial dealings, transfers of assets, business restructurings and cost contribution arrangements. Furthermore, the regulation now categorises “other” financial transactions as a distinct type of RPT. For this newly specified category, PMK-172 provides more detailed guidance on the preparatory analysis that must be undertaken prior to applying transfer pricing methods. These preliminary analyses are an essential component of a sound arm's length evaluation and must be properly completed to support the overall transfer pricing position."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "a16436de-3323-47d5-b5e2-0098ab6e2207",
        "citation_number": 11,
        "cited_text": "Inbound investment and holding structures Where an Indonesian entity is controlled by a foreign holding company, all intercompany transactions with that holding company and other group entities fall within the TP framework. Management fees, shared service charges and royalty payments are frequently challenged by the DGT where the preliminary analysis requirement under PMK-172 is not satisfied. The DGT examines whether the Indonesian entity genuinely received an identifiable service, whether the charge reflects the actual benefit received and whether the selected pricing method is appropriate."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "a16436de-3323-47d5-b5e2-0098ab6e2207",
        "citation_number": 12,
        "cited_text": "Intercompany financing Related-party loans must be priced at arm's length interest rates supported by a preliminary analysis. The DGT may reclassify debt instruments as equity where the debt-to-equity structure deviates from what independent parties would accept, rendering interest deductions non-allowable and recategorising payments as dividends subject to withholding tax. PMK-172 requires specific preliminary analysis documentation for all intercompany financing arrangements. Business restructuring"
      },
      {
        "source_id": "206cb212-7f79-45be-9a17-fa7f2786f648",
        "citation_number": 13,
        "cited_text": "PPN E PKP — IVA INDONESIANA E REGISTRAZIONE GUIDA COMPLETA PER PT PMA IN INDONESIA 2024-2025 Guida normativa verificata | Basata su UU 42/2009 (PPN), UU 7/2021 (HPP), PP 44/2022 Prodotta da Bali Zero / Zantara Intelligence ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ CHE COS'È LA PPN ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ La PPN (Pajak Pertambahan Nilai) è l'IVA indonesiana — un'imposta indiretta sui consumi applicata alla vendita di beni e servizi. [TAX-026]"
