      },
      {
        "source_id": "a16436de-3323-47d5-b5e2-0098ab6e2207",
        "citation_number": 15,
        "cited_text": "Primary and secondary adjustments Where the DGT determines that a controlled transaction does not satisfy the ALP, it issues a primary adjustment to the Indonesian entity's taxable income. A secondary adjustment follows automatically under PMK-172, treating the excess profit as a constructive dividend subject to withholding tax, with a parallel VAT secondary adjustment that compounds the financial exposure. Statute of limitations Under Article 13(1) of the General Tax Provisions Law (UU KUP), as amended by Law No. 7 of 2021 on the Harmonisation of Tax Regulations, the DGT may issue a TP assessment within five years from the end of the relevant tax year. Where a current-year adjustment is agreed, the DGT may seek consistent adjustments across all prior years that remain within the five-year window."
